  "problem": "A company processes and packages three types of rice: rice $A,$ rice $B,$ and rice $C.$ A study by the company's sales analysts demonstrates how consumer preference changes from one kind of rice to another year after year. The table below shows the results of this study.\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rice $A$** | **Rice $B$** | **Rice $C$** |\n| To: | **Rice $A$** | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| **Rice $B$** | $0.2$ | $0.7$ | $0.2$ |  |\n| **Rice $C$** | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.65$ |  |\n\nFor example, $20%$ of the people who preferred rice $B$ last year switched to rice $C$ this year.\n\nIf the company has $200\\,000$ customers and the listed probabilities remain constant over many years, how many customers will eventually purchase rice $B?$",
